<item><title>Three Namibian women earn 50MIA sports nominations</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/three-namibian-women-earn-50mia-sports-nominations-c0957d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/three-namibian-women-earn-50mia-sports-nominations-c0957d/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>Journalists Limba Mupetami and Geneva De Jager and Netball Namibia representative Carol Garoes were nominated across the continental honours.</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:50:55 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" length="33196" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Namibia agriculture grows 17.8% as construction contracts</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-agriculture-grows-17-8-as-construction-contracts-c41cfd/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-agriculture-grows-17-8-as-construction-contracts-c41cfd/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>The farm sector added 0.8 percentage points to second-quarter growth, while construction fell 15.5%, according to the statistics agency.</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:10:24 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" length="33196" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
